      "side": 1,
      "message": "String comparisons are generally frowned upon :)\n\nIf there is a way to do a direct equality comparison, that would be cleaner. The issue with String comparisons is that multiple threads with the same name could end up matching, and that\u0027d still leave us with a race condition.\n\nGenerally, the way this ends up getting done is that we often use HandlerThread(s) and HandlerExecutors, and do Thread.currentThread() \u003d\u003d handerThread.getThread() or something.",
